-- Precedence between instruments, encoded once (MMS-521). Given what each
-- instrument that speaks to a pay item says for a case, it rules which one
-- governs and by which rule. The root (l4/lib/root.l4) calls it for every
-- item; no instrument keeps a copy of it.
--
-- The rules it applies, in this order, are the instruments' own and the
-- law's; none is invented here:
--   1. The takanon's introduction (takanon/terms-service.education.gov.il/
--      terms.l4, `prevails over the takanon`): where the takanon does not
--      match a collective agreement, the law, a Director-General's circular,
--      a Ministry procedure or a more recent circular to the owners, they
--      prevail. If any instrument that prevails over it speaks, the takanon
--      is out; if none does, the takanon governs over the rest.
--   2. Among circulars to the owners left, the later replaces the earlier on
--      the same point (convention precedence.later-circular).
--   3. Among collective agreements, the provision in the employee's favour
--      (the Collective Agreements Law, §23).
--   4. Between an agreement and the term the employer pays by (a circular's
--      figure), the term stands where it is in the employee's favour and the
--      agreement does not forbid it (§22; convention
--      instruments.favourable-circular) — but first, for a budgeted or
--      supported employer, what goes beyond the agreement stands only as far
--      as the Budget Foundations Law §29 permits (convention
--      instruments.section-29-approval). A lower term yields to the agreement:
--      "a circular never out-ranks an agreement" (precedence.agreement).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT collective_agreements_law
IMPORT budget_foundations_law

§ `סדר העדיפות בין המסמכים — מקום אחד לכל הכללים`

§§ `שמות הכללים`

-- The rules a ruling names, each once: a resolution in the root cites the
-- same name, so it cannot drift from what precedence applies.
`§22: a term in the employee's favour stands` MEANS "חוק הסכמים קיבוציים, סעיף 22: תנאי לטובת העובד עומד"
`§29: the excess over the agreement is void` MEANS "חוק יסודות התקציב, סעיף 29: העודף על ההסכם בטל"
`a circular never out-ranks the agreement` MEANS "חוזר אינו גובר על ההסכם שהוא מבצע"
`the only instrument that speaks` MEANS "המסמך היחיד שמדבר"
`the takanon's introduction: nothing that prevails over it speaks` MEANS "מבוא התקנון: אף מסמך שגובר על התקנון אינו מדבר"
`the takanon's introduction: a more recent circular prevails` MEANS "מבוא התקנון: חוזר מאוחר יותר גובר"
`a later circular replaces an earlier one` MEANS "חוזר מאוחר גובר על חוזר מוקדם בעניין אחד"
`§23: the provision in the employee's favour` MEANS "חוק הסכמים קיבוציים, סעיף 23: ההוראה שלטובת העובד"
`the takanon's introduction: an agreement prevails` MEANS "מבוא התקנון: הסכם קיבוצי גובר על התקנון"
`no instrument speaks` MEANS "אין מסמך"

§§ `מסמך וטענתו`

@desc What one instrument says a pay item is, for one case.
DECLARE `claim` HAS
    `by`     IS AN `instrument`
    `answer` IS A NUMBER

@desc Which instrument governs a pay item for a case, what it gives, and by which rule.
DECLARE `ruling` HAS
    `the answer`  IS A NUMBER
    `governed by` IS AN `instrument`
    `by the rule` IS A STRING

GIVEN i IS AN `instrument`, a IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `claim`
DECIDE `the claim of` i a IS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST n THEN JUST (`claim` WITH `by` IS i, `answer` IS n)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§ `1 מבוא התקנון`

GIVEN c IS A `claim`, `the takanon's provision was last amended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim prevails over the takanon` c `the takanon's provision was last amended` IF
    `prevails over the takanon`
        (`conflicting source` WITH
            `source kind`   IS c's `by`'s `kind`
            `source issued` IS c's `by`'s `issued`)
        `the takanon's provision was last amended`

GIVEN claims IS A LIST OF `claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `claim`
DECIDE `the takanon's claims` claims IS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `by`'s `is the takanon`) claims

GIVEN claims IS A LIST OF `claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `claim`
DECIDE `the other instruments' claims` claims IS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD NOT c's `by`'s `is the takanon`) claims

GIVEN claims IS A LIST OF `claim`
      `the takanon's provision was last amended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the takanon stands` claims `the takanon's provision was last amended` IF
        NOT null (`the takanon's claims` claims)
    AND NOT any (GIVEN c YIELD `the claim prevails over the takanon` c `the takanon's provision was last amended`)
                (`the other instruments' claims` claims)

-- What is left once the takanon's introduction has been applied: the
-- takanon alone if it stands, the others if it does not.
GIVEN claims IS A LIST OF `claim`
      `the takanon's provision was last amended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `claim`
DECIDE `the claims the takanon's introduction leaves` claims `the takanon's provision was last amended` IS
    IF `the takanon stands` claims `the takanon's provision was last amended`
    THEN `the takanon's claims` claims
    ELSE `the other instruments' claims` claims

§§ `2 חוזר מאוחר`

GIVEN claims IS A LIST OF `claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `claim`
DECIDE `the agreements' claims` claims IS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `by`'s `kind` EQUALS `a collective agreement`) claims

GIVEN claims IS A LIST OF `claim`
GIVETH A LIST OF `claim`
DECIDE `the employer's claims` claims IS
    filter (GIVEN c YIELD NOT c's `by`'s `kind` EQUALS `a collective agreement`) claims

GIVEN a IS A `claim`, b IS A `claim`
GIVETH A `claim`
DECIDE `the later of` a b IS
    IF DATE_SERIAL (b's `by`'s `issued`) GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL (a's `by`'s `issued`) THEN b ELSE a

GIVEN first IS A `claim`, rest IS A LIST OF `claim`
GIVETH A `claim`
DECIDE `the latest of` first rest IS
    foldr (GIVEN c, acc YIELD `the later of` acc c) first rest

§§ `3 בין הסכמים — סעיף 23`

GIVEN a IS A `claim`, b IS A `claim`
GIVETH A `claim`
DECIDE `the more favourable of` a b IS
    IF `the amount that governs between agreements` (a's `answer`) (b's `answer`) EQUALS a's `answer` THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN first IS A `claim`, rest IS A LIST OF `claim`
GIVETH A `claim`
DECIDE `the most favourable of` first rest IS
    foldr (GIVEN c, acc YIELD `the more favourable of` acc c) first rest

§§ `4 הסכם מול התנאי שהמעסיק משלם לפיו — סעיפים 22 ו־29`

-- The employer, as the Budget Foundations Law tells bodies apart: an
-- owner other than a local authority is taken as a body declared
-- supported, the strictest case (as circular תש"ע/2 does).
GIVEN e IS A `the teacher's employer`
GIVETH AN `employing body`
DECIDE `the body section 29 asks about` e IS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `employed by the State` THEN `the State`
    WHEN `employed by a local authority` THEN `a local authority`
    WHEN `employed by another owning body` THEN `a body declared supported`

-- §29 first: the employer's term, cut back to the agreement's amount where
-- the employer is bound by §29 and the term is neither as practised for all
-- state employees nor approved. Then §22 between the agreement and what
-- stands.
GIVEN agreement IS A `claim`, term IS A `claim`, e IS A `the teacher's employer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what the employer's term gives under section 29` agreement term e IS
    `the amount that stands under section 29`
        (term's `answer`)
        (agreement's `answer`)
        (`section 29 permits the change`
            (`the body section 29 asks about` e)
            (term's `by`'s `practised for all state employees`)
            (term's `by`'s `approved by the Finance Minister`)
            FALSE)

GIVEN agreement IS A `claim`, term IS A `claim`, e IS A `the teacher's employer`
GIVETH A `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling between an agreement and the employer's term` agreement term e IS
    IF      `the amount that governs between agreement and contract` (agreement's `answer`) `what stands` FALSE EQUALS `what stands`
        AND `what stands` GREATER THAN agreement's `answer`
    THEN `ruling` WITH
             `the answer`  IS `what stands`
             `governed by` IS term's `by`
             `by the rule` IS `§22: a term in the employee's favour stands`
    ELSE `ruling` WITH
             `the answer`  IS agreement's `answer`
             `governed by` IS agreement's `by`
             `by the rule` IS (IF term's `answer` GREATER THAN agreement's `answer`
                               THEN `§29: the excess over the agreement is void`
                               ELSE `a circular never out-ranks the agreement`)
    WHERE
        `what stands` MEANS `what the employer's term gives under section 29` agreement term e

§§ `ההכרעה`

GIVEN c IS A `claim`, rule IS A STRING
GIVETH A `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling for` c rule IS
    `ruling` WITH `the answer` IS c's `answer`, `governed by` IS c's `by`, `by the rule` IS rule

-- The one ruling for a pay item and a case: the claims of every instrument
-- that speaks, the employer, and the date the takanon's provision on the
-- item was last amended. NOTHING where no instrument speaks.
GIVEN claims IS A LIST OF `claim`
      e IS A `the teacher's employer`
      `the takanon's provision was last amended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling on` claims e `the takanon's provision was last amended` IS
    CONSIDER `the claims the takanon's introduction leaves` claims `the takanon's provision was last amended`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF `the takanon stands` claims `the takanon's provision was last amended`
        THEN JUST (`the ruling for` first
                       (IF count (`the other instruments' claims` claims) EQUALS 0
                        THEN `the only instrument that speaks`
                        ELSE `the takanon's introduction: nothing that prevails over it speaks`))
        ELSE JUST (`the ruling among` (first FOLLOWED BY rest) e (count (`the takanon's claims` claims) GREATER THAN 0))

GIVEN left IS A LIST OF `claim`
      e IS A `the teacher's employer`
      `the takanon is out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `ruling`
DECIDE `the ruling among` left e `the takanon is out` IS
    CONSIDER `the agreements' claims` left
    WHEN EMPTY THEN
        CONSIDER `the employer's claims` left
        WHEN EMPTY THEN `the ruling for` (`claim` WITH `by` IS `no instrument`, `answer` IS 0) `no instrument speaks`
        WHEN t FOLLOWED BY ts THEN
            `the ruling for` (`the latest of` t ts)
                (IF null ts
                 THEN (IF `the takanon is out` THEN `the takanon's introduction: a more recent circular prevails` ELSE `the only instrument that speaks`)
                 ELSE `a later circular replaces an earlier one`)
    WHEN a FOLLOWED BY more THEN
        CONSIDER `the employer's claims` left
        WHEN EMPTY THEN
            `the ruling for` (`the most favourable of` a more)
                (IF NOT null more
                 THEN `§23: the provision in the employee's favour`
                 ELSE (IF `the takanon is out` THEN `the takanon's introduction: an agreement prevails` ELSE `the only instrument that speaks`))
        WHEN t FOLLOWED BY ts THEN
            `the ruling between an agreement and the employer's term` (`the most favourable of` a more) (`the latest of` t ts) e

`no instrument` MEANS
    `instrument` WITH
        `module`        IS ""
        `title`         IS ""
        `kind`          IS `another source`
        `is the takanon` IS FALSE
        `issued`        IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1900
        `practised for all state employees` IS FALSE
        `approved by the Finance Minister`  IS FALSE
